// ===========================================================================
// MES CELL DATA SERVICE  (SQLite, two-table, one row per cell QR)
//
//   cells_history  ONE row per cell QR code. If the same QR arrives again:
//                    - identical values  -> ignored (read_count++ only)
//                    - different values  -> row UPDATED with latest values
//                                           and re-queued for the MES
//                  Kept for RETENTION_DAYS, then purged automatically.
//
//   cells_queue    working queue, one row per cell waiting to be sent.
//                  Deleted once the MES acknowledges it.
//
// Cells with QR code "NG" or blank are NOT deduplicated -- those are failed
// reads, not identities, and collapsing them would destroy the record.
//
// Requires Node.js 22.13+ (uses the built-in node:sqlite module).
// Run with:  "C:\Software_Tools\new_OCV\node-v24.21.0-win-x64\node.exe" mesCellDataService.js
//
// Query mode (does not start the service):
//   node mesCellDataService.js --find 03HCB00LG6T5BVG6T0992044
//   node mesCellDataService.js --stats
//   node mesCellDataService.js --pending
//   node mesCellDataService.js --purge      (manual run of the same purge)
//   node mesCellDataService.js --vacuum     (reclaim disk space, service OFF)
// ===========================================================================
